1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:01,401
Everyone says
the superstore

2
00:00:01,421 --> 00:00:04,411
is the best place
to survive an outbreak.

3
00:00:04,478 --> 00:00:06,415
Everyone else
says it too.

4
00:00:06,582 --> 00:00:07,339
Six a.m.

5
00:00:07,359 --> 00:00:09,872
Tess was unloading
at the back.

6
00:00:10,089 --> 00:00:11,622
[GUEST] Reports of attacks
downtown.

7
00:00:11,642 --> 00:00:13,379
[GUEST] Officials say
stay indoors.

8
00:00:13,596 --> 00:00:15,059
Minutes later,
the manager

9
00:00:15,079 --> 00:00:17,117
opened the doors
for shelter.

10
00:00:17,334 --> 00:00:19,622
And the whole town
drove in.

11
00:00:19,839 --> 00:00:20,721
Horns. Alarms.

12
00:00:20,741 --> 00:00:22,727
Hundreds of people
shouting.

13
00:00:23,039 --> 00:00:25,798
Tess knew this building
from the back.

14
00:00:25,818 --> 00:00:28,384
One glass front.
Eight dock doors.

15
00:00:28,601 --> 00:00:31,240
[GUEST] Can you get us
out of here?

16
00:00:31,457 --> 00:00:33,176
Inside: food for months.

17
00:00:33,196 --> 00:00:35,988
Outside: a van,
and a road.

18
00:00:36,205 --> 00:00:37,873
No reversing.
No beeping.

19
00:00:37,893 --> 00:00:41,028
She rolled out the back,
lights off.

20
00:00:41,245 --> 00:00:41,967
Behind her,

21
00:00:41,987 --> 00:00:44,766
the town was walking
toward the noise.

22
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:50,272
[GUEST] We left the best
place to survive.

23
00:00:50,589 --> 00:00:52,490
Tess didn't need
the superstore.

24
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,230
She'd been driving one.

